# Each tab comes back to its Space, at its place in the Space's list
# (add-spaces design D6). ClairSpaceTabs records a tab's Space and its index
# in the Space's list as session extra data through
# SessionService::AddTabExtraData whenever they change, and reads them back
# from the restored tab. These hunks only call into
# overlay/chrome/browser/clair/window/clair_space_session.
#
# - session_service_base.cc: the session file's rebuild writes the tags again;
#   it otherwise keeps no tab extra data.
# - browser_live_tab_context.cc: adds the tags to a closing tab's extra data
#   for Reopen Closed Tab and Window.
# - browser_tabrestore.cc: CreateRestoredTab, which session restore and Reopen
#   Closed Tab both use, reads the tags onto the new WebContents before it
#   joins a tab strip.
# - session_restore.cc: beside DropPeeks, drops the tabs on the new tab page
#   and the windows left empty, so a launch adds only its own new tab page
#   (add-profiles design D6).
#
# The tags include the window's group (add-profiles design D6), which the
# same calls carry.

